  "radial_n:right": "too short and too broken to ship under this name: only 18 verified levels (< 20)",
  "artery:right": "FAILED the human check on the montage: the mask does not sit on an arterial lumen. Over all 60 kept levels it outlines a small dark patch (median diameter 2.1 mm, p10 1.8, p90 2.7) lying ON the medial border of the arm's muscle mass at the muscle/fat interface, with no pale arterial wall around it. A brachial artery in a woman is 3.5-5 mm; this is under a third of that area and the wrong appearance, so it is NOT shipped as brachial_a_r."
 },
 "limits": [
  "NOTHING IS SHIPPED UNDER AN ANATOMICAL NAME. All four labels are nulled in the subject mapping with the reason in their notes. The label volume and the montage are kept so the run can be reviewed.",
  "WHY: this cadaver's brachial artery does not photograph as a dark clotted lumen. The femoral/popliteal lumen rule looks for a near-black core (3 mm mean red < 58); her UPPER-ARM muscle photographs at red 44-90, i.e. as dark as a thigh lumen, so that rule finds either nothing or the whole belly. The rule was rewritten for local contrast (a blob at least 35 red levels darker than its own 8 mm neighbourhood, a pale wall at least 30 above it, and a 0.7-2 mm annulus that is at least 35-50% not muscle-red), which does find real vessels in this arm - but inside the deep bundle corridor it yields a median of 0-1 candidates per level and no chain longer than 27 levels.",
  "The only dark vessel that survives the length of this arm anywhere inside the deep-arm hull (144 of 211 levels, y 502 to 359, median diameter 4.1 mm) lies 45 mm ANTERIOR to the humerus centre at the muscle/subcutaneous-fat interface, i.e. OUTSIDE the deep fascia. That is a superficial vein of the arm (cephalic or basilic), not the brachial artery, and it is 45 mm from the bone so the 38 mm bundle corridor refuses it. It is reported here and not shipped: naming it would be a guess.",
  "The three nerves were not found. vhf_nerve_track.nerve_blobs was relaxed for the arm (stand-off 0.7 mm instead of 1 mm, core 2.5 mm2 instead of 4 mm2, because an arm nerve is 3-6 mm and lies in fat) and the walks still held 1, 1 and 18 levels. Their seeds are relations to the tracked artery, which is itself rejected, so they could not have been right either.",
  "The frame IS sound and is what the run contributes: the deep-arm muscle hull separates her arm from the chest wall it touches at these levels (a plain tissue island, as written for the free forearm, runs into the thorax), and the photographed humerus disc was tracked on 182 of 203 levels from y 520 to y 318. The CT humerus label lands a median 8.9 mm off the photographed bone (per level in the report), which is why the CT is only a seed.",
  "Only the RIGHT arm was run. The brachial artery's origin at the lower border of teres major and its division into radial and ulnar arteries in the cubital fossa are not covered.",
  "The tracked vessel mask would in any case be the LUMEN, not the wall, and a cadaveric muscular artery is contracted, so measured diameters under the living 3.5-5 mm would be reported as measured."
 ],
